&gt; The language itself is quite beautiful when used properly and with modern features.<p>I respect your opinion but I wouldn&#x27;t call Java beautiful (of course it depends on your definition of beautiful). It takes so much ceremony to do things you would do without any thought in other languages .<p>Initiating a mutable set<p>Python<p>`a = {1,2}`<p>What most Java programmers do<p>```
var a = new HashSet&lt;&gt;();
a.add(1);
a.add(2);
```<p>Shorter one but requires more ceremony, and hence knowledge of more language semantics<p>```
var a = new HashSet&lt;&gt;(new Arraylist&lt;&gt;(List.of(1,2))
```<p>I don&#x27;t know if the above works but the Idea is to initiate a list and pass it into a HashSet constructor.<p>Similarly Java 21 allows you to model union types but doing so requires you to define N+1 classes where N is the number of union cases whereas in other languages it&#x27;s as simple as `type A = C |D`
